Also treat XDG_SESSION_TYPE as evidence of a graphical session.

oo7-daemon picks between the GNOME prompter (org.gnome.keyring.SystemPrompter)
and a CLI prompter based solely on DISPLAY/WAYLAND_DISPLAY in its own process
environment. Those are exported by the compositor and imported into the systemd
user manager during session startup, but oo7-daemon.service is WantedBy=
default.target, so the manager starts it at session open -- concurrently with
the compositor. A service inherits the manager's environment at start, so the
daemon is permanently stuck with a pre-import copy and falls back to the CLI
prompter for the whole session. Every libsecret caller then fails with:

  CLI prompter failed: NameHasNoOwner: Name
  "org.freedesktop.secrets.CliPrompter" does not exist

It cannot simply be started later: pam_oo7.so auto_start runs in the PAM session
phase and the daemon must already exist to collect the login secret from the
transient oo7-daemon-login helper, so delaying it trades this bug for the loss of
login auto-unlock.

XDG_SESSION_TYPE is set by logind at session open, so it is present in the
daemon's environment even when the display variables are not -- verified on a
running system, where the daemon had XDG_SESSION_TYPE=wayland and
XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=niri but neither DISPLAY nor WAYLAND_DISPLAY. Consulting it
answers the same question ("am I in a graphical session?") without depending on
startup ordering.

Note the existing check only tests these variables for non-emptiness and never
connects to a display, so this widens the same predicate rather than changing
its meaning.

Upstream: https://github.com/linux-credentials/oo7/issues/530 -- stalled since
2026-07-28 with the maintainer unable to reproduce on Fedora, where oo7 is not
the default provider and is D-Bus activated after the session is up rather than
started at default.target. Tracked downstream as starlit-os/krytis#588. Drop this
patch once upstream lands a fix; the maintainer may prefer checking whether a
SystemPrompter name is owned on the bus, which is the question oo7 actually wants
answered.
diff --git a/server/src/service/mod.rs b/server/src/service/mod.rs
index d43c109..8974a30 100644
--- a/server/src/service/mod.rs
+++ b/server/src/service/mod.rs
@@ -530,8 +530,15 @@ impl Service {
             return *override_type;
         }
 
+        // A graphical session may exist even when the compositor's display
+        // variables never reached this process: oo7-daemon starts at
+        // default.target, before the compositor imports them into the systemd
+        // user manager. XDG_SESSION_TYPE comes from logind at session open, so
+        // it is present either way. See krytis#588 / oo7#530.
         let has_display = std::env::var_os("DISPLAY").is_some_and(|v| !v.is_empty())
-            || std::env::var_os("WAYLAND_DISPLAY").is_some_and(|v| !v.is_empty());
+            || std::env::var_os("WAYLAND_DISPLAY").is_some_and(|v| !v.is_empty())
+            || std::env::var_os("XDG_SESSION_TYPE")
+                .is_some_and(|v| v == "wayland" || v == "x11");
 
         if has_display {
             #[cfg(any(feature = "plasma_native_crypto", feature = "plasma_openssl_crypto"))]
